            <ArticleTitle>Exercise and the patient with Type I diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>665-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the clinical features of heart disease in the diabetic in three categories: (1) coronary atherosclerosis (CAD), (2) autonomic neuropathy, and (3) cardiomyopathy. Particular attention is given to current methods of noninvasive assessment of cardiac function in juvenile diabetics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
